📊 STUDENT MARK ANALYSIS SYSTEM
A Student Mark Analysis System helps teachers analyze class performance by calculating average marks, finding toppers, counting pass/fail students, sorting marks, searching for specific marks, and updating marks dynamically.

💡 Example:
5 students with marks: 78 85 92 67 88

Average: (78 + 85 + 92 + 67 + 88) / 5 = 82.0

Highest: 92 at position 2

Lowest: 67 at position 3

Pass (≥75): 4 students (78, 85, 92, 88)

Fail (<75): 1 student (67)

Sorted: 67 78 85 88 92

Top 3: 92 88 85

→ Complete analysis generated! ✅

Given N students and their marks, perform complete analysis including average, highest/lowest, pass/fail count, sorting, searching, and updating marks.

📥 Input Format
First line: Integer N (number of students)

Second line: N space-separated integers (marks of each student)

Then interactive input for search and update operations

📌 Constraints
1 ≤ N ≤ 100

0 ≤ Marks ≤ 100

All marks are integers

Pass mark is 75

📤 Output Format
Print Original Marks

Print Class Average (1 decimal place)

Print Highest Mark

Print Lowest Mark

Print Topper Position (0-based index)

Print Pass Count (marks ≥ 75)

Print Fail Count (marks < 75)

Print Sorted Marks (ascending order)

Print Top 3 Students marks

Search Operation:

Prompt: "Enter mark to search: "

Print mark positions or "Mark not found"

Update Operation:

Prompt: "Enter position to update: "

Prompt: "Enter extra marks: "

Print Updated Marks

🧪 Sample Input 0
text
5
78 85 92 67 88
✅ Sample Output 0
text
Original Marks: 78 85 92 67 88

Class Average: 82.0
Highest Mark: 92
Lowest Mark: 67
Topper Position: 2

Pass Count: 4
Fail Count: 1

Sorted Marks: 67 78 85 88 92

Top 3 Students: 92 88 85

Enter mark to search: 85
Mark 85 found at position: 1

Enter position to update: 2
Enter extra marks: 5
Updated Marks: 78 85 97 67 88

🏷️ Difficulty Level
🔵 Easy


Happy Coding! 💻✨


